  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=2.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(-3{t}^{2}+6t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(-{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[-(2)^{3}+3(2)^{2}]-[-(0)^{3}+3(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[-8+12]-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
